meta {
  name: Approve Booking Request
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/booking-requests/{{bookingRequestId}}/approve
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {}
}

docs {
  Creates the appointment in one transaction: the contact's single active match (reactivated if
  inactive, otherwise untouched; for a number, only a single trusted match), else a new PORTAL patient
  from the request; the consent with the request's original time and evidence; a CONFIRMED appointment
  with a reminder on the patient's channel. The patient
  gets the confirmation (for a virtual location once the Meet link is ready).

  `{ "existingPatientId": "<uuid>" }` picks one of the active candidates, which a shared number needs.
  `{ "restorePatientId": "<uuid>" }` restores one of the deleted candidates instead (409 while an active
  patient holds the email; a number may be shared). At most one of the two; 404 for an id that is not a
  candidate. Picking a record whose number this request proved clears its unverified flag. 409 "Booking request is no longer pending" for a resolved
  or expired request; a slot conflict is also 409 and leaves the request PENDING. Cookie requests
  need `X-CSRF-Token`.
}
